---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FigureWithCaption from '../components/FigureWithCaption.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research"
  description="Research themes in top-quark spin correlations, quantum information, quantum annealing reconstruction, and machine learning for particle physics."
>
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
    My work connects collider measurements, quantum information, and machine-learning methods for
    reconstruction and anomaly detection. The common thread is turning complex collision data into
    observables, assignments, and model outputs whose assumptions can be inspected.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8">
    <section aria-labelledby="top-quark-heading">
      <h2 id="top-quark-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Top-Quark Spin Correlations</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        Top quarks decay before they hadronize, so their decay products preserve information about
        the spin state of the produced top-antitop pair. I work on measurements and interpretation
        tools for spin-correlation matrices, entanglement-sensitive observables, and the phase-space
        regions where collider data can test quantum behavior at TeV energies.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <FigureWithCaption
          src="/images/research-top-spin.svg"
          alt="Diagram of a top-antitop event with lepton analyzers, spin axes, a correlation matrix, and an entanglement-sensitive threshold observable."
          caption="Top-pair spin analyses infer a production density matrix from decay angles, then summarize the spin-dependent terms as correlation coefficients and entanglement-sensitive observables."
        />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <a class="underline" href="/demos/spin-explorer/">Open the Spin Correlation Explorer</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="quantum-heading">
      <h2 id="quantum-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Quantum Computing</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        My quantum-computing work is grounded in high-energy physics use cases: quantum-information
        observables in top-quark pairs and quantum-annealing formulations of reconstruction
        problems. A representative example is primary-vertex reconstruction, where charged-particle
        tracks are encoded as an optimization problem and the solution assigns tracks to candidate
        collision vertices.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <FigureWithCaption
          src="/images/quantum-workflow.svg"
          alt="Detector-track diagram mapped into weighted pair connections, a QUBO matrix, annealer embedding, and vertex clusters."
          caption="Quantum-annealing reconstruction converts track compatibility into a QUBO objective; the resulting bit assignment groups tracks into primary-vertex candidates."
        />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <a class="underline" href="/publications/?tag=quantum">Browse quantum-tagged publications</a
        >
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ml-heading">
      <h2 id="ml-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Machine Learning</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        Machine-learning projects focus on particle-physics discovery workflows, including
        foundation-model representations, anomaly-detection challenges, and transparent evaluation.
        The emphasis is not just predictive performance: model outputs need benchmark context,
        uncertainty checks, and documentation that states which physics tasks the model is meant to
        support.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <FigureWithCaption
          src="/images/ml-model-card.svg"
          alt="Diagram showing detector events encoded by a foundation model, evaluated with anomaly metrics, stress tests, and model-card documentation."
          caption="Foundation-model studies separate reusable event representations from downstream anomaly scores, benchmark metrics, shifted-sample checks, and model-card limitations."
        />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <a class="underline" href="/talks/?tag=machine%20learning">Browse machine-learning talks</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
